<code>assert (e == null) => (this.peekLast() == null); assert (e != null) => (this.peekLast().equals(e));</code>

However, since we need a single assert statement, we can combine these two conditions using a logical OR:

<code>assert (e == null) == (this.peekLast() == null);</code>

This single assert statement captures both conditions: if the added element `e` is null, then the last element of the list (`this.peekLast()`) should also be null, and if `e` is not null, then the last element of the list should be equal to `e`.
